1
00:00:00,096 --> 00:00:01,056
It's summer vacation!

2
00:00:01,056 --> 00:00:05,350
Beelu visits the old street he's been looking forward to seeing.

3
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:06,625
His mom once told him

4
00:00:06,625 --> 00:00:07,750
this place

5
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:09,024
was full of old-world charm.

6
00:00:09,024 --> 00:00:10,752
But when he arrives,

7
00:00:10,752 --> 00:00:12,000
Beelu feels

8
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,208
that although the place is steeped in history,

9
00:00:14,208 --> 00:00:16,032
it also feels like a shopping district.

10
00:00:16,032 --> 00:00:17,328
Beelu feels

11
00:00:17,328 --> 00:00:19,440
something about it seems strange, but he can't put his finger on it.

12
00:00:23,725 --> 00:00:26,620
Come one, come all! Don't miss out!

13
00:00:26,620 --> 00:00:27,800
Hello! I'm Little Deer.

14
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,664
Would you like to buy a little toy, friend?

15
00:00:30,664 --> 00:00:31,264
Wow!

16
00:00:31,264 --> 00:00:31,888
Suddenly,

17
00:00:31,888 --> 00:00:33,050
a deer comes running over

18
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:35,152
and starts trying to sell Beelu something.

19
00:00:35,152 --> 00:00:37,360
Beelu is startled.

20
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:40,048
Little Deer looks around Beelu

21
00:00:40,048 --> 00:00:42,400
and suddenly changes his attitude completely.

22
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:43,744
Sigh...

23
00:00:43,744 --> 00:00:45,808
Your mom and dad aren't here?

24
00:00:45,808 --> 00:00:47,872
Then no one can pay for you.

25
00:00:47,872 --> 00:00:50,176
I need to save up money to build an amusement park!

26
00:00:50,176 --> 00:00:52,720
See ya!

27
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,406
Hearing Little Deer say this,

28
00:00:54,406 --> 00:00:56,896
Beelu is completely confused.

29
00:00:56,896 --> 00:01:00,016
Why do you want to build an amusement park here?

30
00:01:00,016 --> 00:01:02,704
Because it'll make money faster, of course!

31
00:01:02,704 --> 00:01:04,432
Beelu gets angry.

32
00:01:04,432 --> 00:01:07,648
How can you build an amusement park at a historic site?

33
00:01:07,648 --> 00:01:08,925
That's awful!

34
00:01:08,925 --> 00:01:10,864
You must not understand this place,

35
00:01:10,864 --> 00:01:12,160
or you wouldn't think that way.

36
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:13,024
That's not true!

37
00:01:13,024 --> 00:01:14,176
I know this place really well.

38
00:01:14,176 --> 00:01:15,900
Why don't you quiz me?

39
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,200
Bring it on!

40
00:01:21,598 --> 00:01:23,441
They butt heads,

41
00:01:23,441 --> 00:01:25,486
neither one willing to back down.

42
00:01:25,486 --> 00:01:27,982
Do you know where this is?

43
00:01:27,982 --> 00:01:29,470
Mōrǔ Xiàng.

44
00:01:29,470 --> 00:01:31,246
I walk through here all the time.

45
00:01:31,246 --> 00:01:32,440
This narrow alley

46
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:36,425
would make a great haunted-house passage for an amusement park, right?

47
00:01:36,425 --> 00:01:39,125
As for the name Mōrǔ Xiàng,

48
00:01:39,125 --> 00:01:40,626
there are several different explanations.

49
00:01:40,626 --> 00:01:41,902
My favorite one is...

50
00:01:41,902 --> 00:01:44,254
Little Deer talks on and on.

51
00:01:44,254 --> 00:01:46,174
Beelu refuses to back down.

52
00:01:48,001 --> 00:01:49,633
As they walk along the old street,

53
00:01:49,633 --> 00:01:50,881
Beelu notices

54
00:01:50,881 --> 00:01:53,250
that the building looks like one his mom told him about.

55
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:55,900
You know what?

56
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:57,361
This is a Minnan-style building!

57
00:01:57,361 --> 00:01:59,377
I know!

58
00:01:59,377 --> 00:02:02,869
You don't see many red-brick houses like this anymore.

59
00:02:02,869 --> 00:02:04,675
It also has beautiful wooden windows,

60
00:02:04,675 --> 00:02:06,375
and the inside is actually quite spacious.

61
00:02:06,375 --> 00:02:08,898
It would make a great visitor center for an amusement park.

62
00:02:08,898 --> 00:02:11,000
Little Deer rattles on again.

63
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,529
Beelu thinks

64
00:02:12,529 --> 00:02:14,545
this time Little Deer just got lucky.

65
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:17,217
They arrive at an old temple.

66
00:02:17,217 --> 00:02:19,909
Little Deer is chatting away.

67
00:02:19,909 --> 00:02:22,972
The area is packed with people.

68
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:26,683
There was an earthquake once

69
00:02:26,683 --> 00:02:29,841
that badly damaged the temple roof.

70
00:02:29,841 --> 00:02:32,650
My dad and the other craftsmen

71
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:34,967
carefully rebuilt it, brick by brick,

72
00:02:34,967 --> 00:02:37,655
and that's how it came to look the way it does now.

73
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:42,431
Little Deer tells the story so well

74
00:02:42,431 --> 00:02:46,384
that passersby clap for him.

75
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:50,725
This place would be perfect for a theme park!

76
00:02:53,736 --> 00:02:55,656
You really know this place well.

77
00:02:55,656 --> 00:02:56,375
But I think...

78
00:02:56,375 --> 00:02:57,672
Of course!

79
00:02:57,672 --> 00:03:01,825
How about giving me a little tip?

80
00:03:01,825 --> 00:03:04,201
Beelu thinks Little Deer's explanation

81
00:03:04,201 --> 00:03:07,000
is as entertaining as a street performance.

82
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,724
So he takes out some money.

83
00:03:08,724 --> 00:03:09,732
Suddenly,

84
00:03:09,732 --> 00:03:12,180
someone taps Little Deer on the head.

85
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:14,532
It's Little Deer's grandma.

86
00:03:14,532 --> 00:03:15,492
Little Deer!

87
00:03:15,492 --> 00:03:18,420
You mustn't ask people for money like that!

88
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:19,044
Whoa!

89
00:03:19,044 --> 00:03:19,664
Grandma!

90
00:03:19,664 --> 00:03:21,396
No, it's not like that! I was...

91
00:03:24,825 --> 00:03:26,505
No, Grandma.

92
00:03:26,505 --> 00:03:28,953
Little Deer said he'd take me to get something tasty.

93
00:03:28,953 --> 00:03:31,025
I was just giving him the money in advance.

94
00:03:31,025 --> 00:03:32,313
Uh, yeah!

95
00:03:32,313 --> 00:03:34,617
I'll take him to get temple-side vermicelli!

96
00:03:34,617 --> 00:03:35,577
Let's go.

97
00:03:35,577 --> 00:03:37,545
Uh, friend...

98
00:03:37,545 --> 00:03:38,793
Friend?

99
00:03:38,793 --> 00:03:40,521
My name's Beelu!

100
00:03:40,521 --> 00:03:43,017
Little Deer awkwardly puts his arm around Beelu

101
00:03:43,017 --> 00:03:45,129
and quickly hurries away from his grandma.

102
00:03:47,450 --> 00:03:48,750
It's super delicious!

103
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:50,400
Right? I'm telling you,

104
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:52,839
Lukang has lots of other great food, too.

105
00:03:52,839 --> 00:03:54,893
Little Deer enthusiastically

106
00:03:54,893 --> 00:03:56,461
tells Beelu all sorts of things about the area.

107
00:03:56,461 --> 00:03:59,213
Beelu listens, fascinated.

108
00:04:00,525 --> 00:04:02,016
After they finish their noodles,

109
00:04:02,016 --> 00:04:03,600
the two walk down the street.

110
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:05,250
Hey, can I ask you something?

111
00:04:05,250 --> 00:04:07,488
Why did you help me back there?

112
00:04:07,488 --> 00:04:10,272
I don't know, either.

113
00:04:10,272 --> 00:04:11,712
But, Little Deer,

114
00:04:11,712 --> 00:04:14,375
I still think building an amusement park is strange.

115
00:04:14,375 --> 00:04:15,360
How come?

116
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:17,616
It would make the old street more prosperous.

117
00:04:19,646 --> 00:04:20,462
Little Deer,

118
00:04:20,462 --> 00:04:22,334
do you like the old street?

119
00:04:22,334 --> 00:04:24,686
Of course I do!

120
00:04:24,686 --> 00:04:26,558
I like the old street, too.

121
00:04:26,558 --> 00:04:28,574
If they build an amusement park,

122
00:04:28,574 --> 00:04:29,918
will the houses here

123
00:04:29,918 --> 00:04:32,078
be torn down?

124
00:04:33,250 --> 00:04:35,945
Little Deer had never thought about that.

125
00:04:35,945 --> 00:04:37,865
He loves the old street.

126
00:04:37,865 --> 00:04:40,169
He doesn't want it torn down, either.

127
00:04:41,150 --> 00:04:42,475
But...

128
00:04:42,475 --> 00:04:44,587
Grandma works so hard.

129
00:04:44,587 --> 00:04:47,675
We could make lots of money if we opened an amusement park.

130
00:04:47,675 --> 00:04:51,403
Then Grandma wouldn't have to work so hard making incense.

131
00:04:51,403 --> 00:04:53,875
Little Deer's family has been making incense for generations.

132
00:04:53,875 --> 00:04:55,800
They insist on making by hand

133
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:57,175
the incense sticks used for worship.

134
00:04:57,175 --> 00:05:00,247
Their family isn't well-off right now.

135
00:05:00,247 --> 00:05:03,307
There are so many things to consider.

136
00:05:03,307 --> 00:05:05,755
Little Deer can't think of an answer

137
00:05:05,755 --> 00:05:08,059
and falls into deep thought.

138
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:10,246
Just then,

139
00:05:10,246 --> 00:05:13,078
Little Deer's grandma happens to walk by.

140
00:05:13,078 --> 00:05:14,806
Hello, ma'am.

141
00:05:14,806 --> 00:05:17,686
Hello there, little one.

142
00:05:17,686 --> 00:05:18,838
Little Deer told me

143
00:05:18,838 --> 00:05:20,422
you make incense, Grandma.

144
00:05:20,422 --> 00:05:22,390
Could I watch you making it?

145
00:05:22,390 --> 00:05:24,502
I'm really interested!

146
00:05:24,502 --> 00:05:26,806
Of course!

147
00:05:26,806 --> 00:05:30,214
Little Deer's grandma readily agrees.

148
00:05:30,214 --> 00:05:32,278
Beelu visits Little Deer's home

149
00:05:32,278 --> 00:05:34,054
and learns about the traditional craft of incense-making.

150
00:05:34,054 --> 00:05:37,075
He has a wonderful time.

151
00:05:37,075 --> 00:05:38,975
Wow!

152
00:05:38,975 --> 00:05:41,158
Seeing Beelu holding the incense sticks,

153
00:05:41,158 --> 00:05:43,462
with his eyes sparkling,

154
00:05:43,462 --> 00:05:46,198
makes Little Deer's grandma smile.

155
00:05:46,198 --> 00:05:49,425
When people hold the incense I make

156
00:05:49,425 --> 00:05:51,500
and pray sincerely to the gods,

157
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:54,934
it makes me feel very proud.

158
00:05:54,934 --> 00:05:56,134
If I can,

159
00:05:56,134 --> 00:06:00,022
I'd like to keep doing this here on the old street.

160
00:06:00,022 --> 00:06:01,556
This is the first time Little Deer has heard

161
00:06:01,556 --> 00:06:03,862
his grandma say that.

162
00:06:03,862 --> 00:06:05,700
It turns out everyone has

163
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:07,750
their own ideas about the old street.

164
00:06:07,750 --> 00:06:08,662
Maybe

165
00:06:08,662 --> 00:06:11,734
the old street doesn't have to be just one thing.

166
00:06:11,734 --> 00:06:14,230
Little Deer suddenly understands.

167
00:06:14,230 --> 00:06:15,478
Little Deer walks over

168
00:06:15,478 --> 00:06:18,550
and says to his grandma and Beelu,

169
00:06:18,550 --> 00:06:20,470
I'll help out, too!

170
00:06:20,470 --> 00:06:24,086
Oh my, that's a surprise!

171
00:06:24,086 --> 00:06:26,250
I just felt like it!

172
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:29,990
The three of them happily get along and work together.

173
00:06:31,050 --> 00:06:33,025
The sky grows dark.

174
00:06:33,025 --> 00:06:35,450
Beelu has to go home.

175
00:06:35,450 --> 00:06:37,000
Little Deer and his grandma

176
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,782
say goodbye to him at the station.

177
00:06:39,782 --> 00:06:40,850
Thank you!

178
00:06:40,850 --> 00:06:43,050
I'll be going now!

179
00:06:43,050 --> 00:06:45,373
Take care on your way!

180
00:06:48,550 --> 00:06:51,669
Today was so much fun!
